text:
**Review Result**
Score: **5/10**. The code is fairly readable and scoped, with useful unit tests on paper, but I would not call it production-ready. The biggest problem is operational: a clean checkout cannot run the advertised pipeline because the story dataset is absent and `generate-stories` depends on a missing manifest. There are also several silent data-quality and numerical edge cases that can produce misleading research outputs.

I could not run the test suite successfully in this environment because dependencies are not installed (`numpy`, `yaml`, package import). Syntax compilation passed when using a temp pycache prefix.

**Bottom Line**
I would **not approve** this as-is. I’d want the clean-checkout workflow fixed, manifest/data validation added, and the model/token edge cases covered before active development resumes.

Estimated rewrite/significant-change scope: **320 LOC**.

```json
{
  "score": 5,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "config.yaml",
      "lines": "11-14",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Default pipeline points at data/stories, but the checkout has no story files, so extraction/demo cannot run from clean state."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/cli.py",
      "lines": "54-58",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "generate-stories requires loading data/stories/manifest.json before generation, making first-time dataset generation impossible."
    },
    {
      "file": "tests/test_datasets.py",
      "lines": "44-51",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "The only story dataset test is skipped when data is missing, so CI can pass while the advertised demo path is broken."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/model.py",
      "lines": "55-59",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "from_pretrained uses dtype while the declared transformers minimum may require torch_dtype, risking runtime incompatibility."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/model.py",
      "lines": "123-125",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "mean_activations can divide by zero for one-token inputs because effective_start can equal sequence length."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/model.py",
      "lines": "171",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "all_token_activations always drops token 0 as BOS without checking offsets, which corrupts activations for tokenizers that do not add BOS."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/vectors.py",
      "lines": "66-70",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "pca_components divides by total variance without handling zero-variance inputs, producing NaNs for constant neutral activations."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/stories.py",
      "lines": "87-90",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "parse_story_block treats any preamble before the first <NEW STORY> delimiter as a story, contaminating generated datasets."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/stories.py",
      "lines": "136",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Story generation HTTP calls have no timeout, so a stalled API request can hang the pipeline indefinitely."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/extract.py",
      "lines": "99-110",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "load_vectors trusts stale artifacts without validating manifest compatibility with the current config or loaded model."
    },
    {
      "file": "emovec/validate.py",
      "lines": "87-90",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Logit-lens markdown writes raw decoded tokens into table cells, so tokens containing pipes or newlines can corrupt the report."
    },
    {
      "file": ".gitignore",
      "lines": "1-3",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Generated outputs and egg-info are ignored but present in the workspace, which makes source vs artifact ownership ambiguous."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 320,
  "approve": false
}
